PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2} 

The C1-C2 black group has exactly two liberties (B1, B2) and can connect to the adjacent B3-B4 group only via B2. White's move at B2 fills that connection point and leaves the C1-C2 group with a single liberty at B1. On Black's reply Black cannot occupy B1 without self-capture and has no other escape or capture that saves the stones, so White takes B1 on the next turn and captures.  

Any other first move (including B1) permits Black to occupy B2, linking the groups into a single chain that cannot be forced into capture. Hence only B2 initiates a line that captures regardless of Black's replies.

